<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 1: Publish the document and point the number at it</h2>
	<p>Replace the locations, area codes, and numbers with your own. Then publish it at <a href="{{ site.voicemlPublisherUrl }}">voiceml.org</a> and set the <code>/r/</code> URL it returns as the phone number&rsquo;s voice URL. Keep the URL exactly as returned, <code>key</code> included, and don&rsquo;t post it publicly.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">main.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["pollos-locations"].main | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 2: Test it</h2>
	<p>Call from a phone whose area code is on your list, and that location rings without a menu. Call from any other phone, and you hear the menu; press a key, and that location rings.</p>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How the routing works</h2>
	<p><code>From</code> is the caller&rsquo;s number in E.164, such as <code>+15055551234</code>. For North American numbers, the first two characters are <code>+1</code> and the next three are the area code, so two <code>slice</code> filters split it:</p>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>How the document reads the caller&rsquo;s number</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Liquid</th>
					<th scope="col">For <code>+15055551234</code></th>
					<th scope="col">For <code>+442071234567</code></th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>{% raw %}From | slice: 0, 2{% endraw %}</code></td><td><code>+1</code></td><td><code>+4</code></td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>{% raw %}From | slice: 2, 3{% endraw %}</code></td><td><code>505</code></td><td><code>207</code>, discarded because the number isn&rsquo;t <code>+1</code></td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>A <code>{% raw %}{% case %}{% endraw %}</code> on the area code sets the restaurant&rsquo;s name and number, and <code>&lt;Number&gt;{% raw %}{{ line }}{% endraw %}&lt;/Number&gt;</code> dials it. Several area codes can share a restaurant in one <code>when</code>, as Arizona&rsquo;s five do for Phoenix.</p>
	<p>When nothing matches, the menu&rsquo;s <code>&lt;Gather&gt;</code> has no <code>action</code>, so the key comes back to the same document as <code>Digits</code>. A <code>{% raw %}{% case Digits %}{% endraw %}</code> near the top replaces the area code with the chosen restaurant&rsquo;s, and the same routing runs again.</p>
</section>

