<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Limits of this design</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>An area code isn&rsquo;t a location.</strong> Mobile numbers keep their area code when people move, so a caller from Phoenix with an Albuquerque number reaches Albuquerque.</li>
		<li><strong>No city or state from the network.</strong> The VoiceML runtime sends <code>FromCity</code>, <code>FromState</code>, and the other location fields empty, so the area code is the only clue in the call.</li>
		<li><strong>The list is fixed in the document.</strong> A new location or area code means publishing again and pointing the number at the new URL.</li>
		<li><strong>Closed restaurants still ring.</strong> To skip a location outside its hours, combine this with the checks in the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-business-hours-routing-with-voiceml/">business-hours example</a>.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

